{
 "schema": 1,
 "name": "analytical-method-validation",
 "description": "Plans, executes, and documents validation, verification, and transfer of analytical procedures under the governing framework - ICH Q2(R2) and Q14, USP <1220>/<1225>/<1226>, ICH M10 bioanalytical, CLSI EP, or ISO/IEC 17025. Use for HPLC, LC-MS/MS, GC, CE, ICP-MS, dissolution, qNMR, qPCR, NIR, and ligand binding or cell-based assays whenever the question is whether a procedure is fit for its intended purpose. Triggers include \"method validation\", \"analytical method validation\", \"AMV\", \"validation protocol\", \"acceptance criteria\", \"linearity\", \"reportable range\", \"accuracy and precision\",…",
 "license": "MIT",
 "compatibility": "Requires Python 3.11+. Scripts use only the standard library - no numpy, scipy, or network access. Statistical distributions are computed from first principles so results are reproducible in any conforming interpreter.",
